Subject: [PATCH 9/11] regulator: qcom: support nested RPM-SMD resources

Add a resource parent for the direct nested layout used by the Khaje reference
FDT. Dispatch qcom,rpm-smd-regulator children by their voltage-key properties:
aggregate vlvl/vfl votes across clients and active/sleep sets, while matching
physical PM6125 rails to the existing regulator table using both regulator-name
and the containing RPM resource type/ID. Preserve the conventional PMIC
container path and its active-set behavior, remove the global RPM handle, and
roll back already-sent physical votes when a later selected set fails.

Static matching against topaz-live-reference.dts covered all six resource names,
30 resource parents, 25 enabled physical PM6125 children, and 8 enabled level
children; every enabled physical child matched its existing PM6125 table
resource type/ID, while disabled PMIC children sharing level-resource
compatibles were not registered. This is static review only: no compilation,
DT schema validation, dtbs_check, or boot test has been run.

